<speak>
<s>This is your Jumu'ah briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">17042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran's power grid serves eighty-eight million people... and the United States Defense Secretary has threatened to bomb it.</s> <s>Pete Hegseth said Washington will hold the Hormuz blockade as long as it takes and strike Iranian electricity if Tehran rejects a nuclear deal.</s> <s>The ceasefire expires on the twenty-second of April, and the Islamabad talks have no confirmed resumption date.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Washington declared a Lebanon ceasefire this week... but the phone call meant to seal it never happened.</s> <s>Mada Masr reconstructs how the announcement was delayed so Donald Trump could broker a conversation between President Aoun and Prime Minister Netanyahu — a call two governments have avoided for thirty-four years.</s> <s>Lebanon declined, Israel's occupation of the south remains unresolved, and Tehran has quietly tied the truce to ongoing nuclear talks.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's army chief flew to Tehran this week to mediate between Iran and the United States.</s> <s>Islamabad hosted the last round of talks, which ended without a deal, and Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif has since lobbied Gulf capitals to hold the line.</s> <s>Trump said he may travel to Islamabad himself to sign a deal, if one can be reached before the ceasefire expires next week.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>American forces left their last Syrian base on Thursday, closing an eleven-year partnership with the Kurdish-led Syrian Democratic Forces.</s> <s>The Kurds have now been folded into Syria's national army, with no written American guarantee of their autonomy.</s> <s>Turkey, which spent a decade opposing that partnership, is now Syria's dominant northern neighbour — and its leverage over Kurdish political life has never been greater.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pope Leo, speaking inside Cameroon's nine-year Anglophone insurgency, called world leaders who spend billions on war while denying resources for healing "a handful of tyrants."</s> <s>More than six thousand people have died in Bamenda's shadow conflict, a war the West has largely ignored.</s> <s>Trump's recent attacks on Leo have drawn dismay across Africa, where the new pope draws his broadest support.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India's opposition alliance boycotted the election for deputy chairman of the upper house, refusing to legitimise a third term for the ruling party's candidate Harivansh.</s> <s>The post has historically required cross-party consensus; this is the first time a sitting presidential appointee has taken it.</s> <s>The Lok Sabha deputy speaker's chair has meanwhile sat empty for years — small vacancies that together hollow out the architecture of Indian democracy.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Sudan's Sovereignty Council sent its envoy to Washington this week, meeting Senator Ted Cruz's office to urge Republicans to choke the weapons reaching the Rapid Support Forces.</s> <s>General Burhan's government is betting that a Republican Congress can be moved where a Democratic White House could not.</s> <s>Sudan's war is entering its third year, and Washington has yet to respond.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Jet fuel in Nigeria has risen two hundred and seventy percent since February, from nine hundred naira a litre to three thousand three hundred.</s> <s>Domestic carriers say they'll ground their fleets on Monday — in a country where Dangote is the sole domestic producer and made no deliveries in March.</s> <s>West Africa's busiest aviation market is about to go dark, and the mechanism is a refining monopoly that the state chose not to break.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Ecuador will impose one hundred percent tariffs on Colombian goods from the first of May, and the rupture is already reshaping the frontier.</s> <s>Criminal groups are moving into the governance vacuum — smuggling, extortion, and protection rackets filling the space where two states are withdrawing cooperation.</s> <s>It's the same pattern that drives illicit economies from the Sahel to Myanmar... disputed territory becoming a subsidy for organised crime.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Slovakia has threatened to veto the European Union's twentieth sanctions package against Russia unless Ukraine reopens the Druzhba pipeline.</s> <s>Bratislava still runs on Russian crude, and EU sanctions require unanimity — one capital can stall the bloc.</s> <s>Ambassadors meet today, and if Slovakia holds, Moscow faces no new restrictions this spring.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Europe's Rosalind Franklin rover finally has a ride to Mars.</s> <s>The European Space Agency cancelled its Russian partnership after the invasion of Ukraine, leaving finished hardware idle for four years; a SpaceX Falcon Heavy will now launch it from Kennedy Space Center as soon as late twenty twenty-eight.</s> <s>The structural lesson is older than any rocket — political rupture becomes lost decades of science when agencies depend on partner launchers.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The biologists who pioneered today's blockbuster weight-loss drugs now say their target was wrong.</s> <s>A new experimental compound in Munich, aimed at GIP and glucagon receptors rather than <sub alias="G L P one">GLP-1</sub>, matched weight loss in primate studies without nausea.</s> <s>If the hypothesis survives human trials, it would challenge a drug pipeline worth tens of billions... and return the question of appetite to first principles.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>China's grid operators poured twenty-four and a half billion dollars into transmission in the first quarter of this year — and still the system is saturating.</s> <s>Solar utilisation fell to ninety point eight percent in early twenty twenty-six, approaching the floor below which new panels cannot be absorbed.</s> <s>Six provinces are now under review, and the world's largest renewables build-out is hitting a ceiling not of ambition but of wires.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Two men were sentenced in Newark this week for running North Korean laptop farms on American soil.</s> <s>Racks of US-domiciled machines let Pyongyang's coders pose as remote American employees, generating more than five million dollars for the regime.</s> <s>The operation's Korean beneficiaries remain beyond US jurisdiction — and the hiring stack that missed them is the one most Western companies still use.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Hackers have deployed new espionage malware, dubbed AgingFly, against Ukrainian hospitals and local governments.</s> <s>The systems targeted are the same ones treating casualties from an active front, and researchers have not yet publicly named the actor behind the campaign.</s> <s>Ukrainian hospital networks remain exposed, in sha'Allah only briefly.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Grupo Seguritech operates one hundred and eighty-eight command centres across Mexico, and it's now expanding north to the US border.</s> <s>From a home-alarm company in nineteen ninety-five, it has built a one point two seven billion dollar empire with thirty-one subsidiaries and deep government contracts.</s> <s>No independent body audits its access to surveillance data — in a country ranked among the world's most dangerous for journalists who might try.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>